    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="d310-01" n="1" xml:id="d310-01"/>

                <head>310. Telegram 201141 From the Department of State to the Embassy in
                        India<anchor n="1" xml:id="d310-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d310-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1972-11-04T00:22:00+00:00">November 4, 1972, 0022Z</date>
                </dateline>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subj:</label>
                    <item>Indian Debt Rescheduling</item>
                </list>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item> USG has decided to participate for one year rpt one year in World Bank
                        proposal for debt relief for India with US share of $29.12 million.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>We have informed World Bank of this decision as part of our continuing
                        technical discussions with bank. Bank is informing Indians and other
                        AID-India Consortium members.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Pending further guidance Embassy should avoid any interpretive comment
                        regarding this decision in discussions with Indian officials. Embassy should
                        not rpt not issue press statement and should restrict response to possible
                        press queries to simple confirmation that decision made.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d310-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d310-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files 1970–73, AID (US) 9 INDIA.
                    Confidential; Immediate. Drafted on November 3 by Schneider; cleared in the
                    Office of International Finance and Development of the Bureau of Economic and
                    Business Affairs by John Gervers, and in the Office of Planning and Development
                    of AID’s Bureau for Asia by Alfred D. White; and approved by Meyer.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d310-f2" n="2" xml:id="d310-f2-content">
                <p>The U.S. agreed to participate with the other members of the India Consortium in
                    restructuring India’s foreign debt.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
